{"meta":{"title":"Record research-cell efficiencies by technology","description":"Milestone record efficiencies of small research solar cells, by technology family, from 1954 to 2026. Shape: data.series is an array of { id, label, short (label for direct chart labels), family, colour (a CSS custom property from odyssey.css), limit (theoretical efficiency limit in % or null), limit_source, note }; data.points is an array of { tech (a series id), year, efficiency (% under the standard AM1.5 global spectrum at 1 sun unless 'suns' is given), institution, area_cm2 (optional), suns (optional, concentration ratio), certified_by (optional test centre), notes (optional), source (a bibliography id) }. Points are milestones, not every record: each one is independently verified against the primary paper, the certifying lab's or institution's announcement, or the Solar cell efficiency tables. Families with no verifiable dated milestone (multicrystalline and amorphous silicon, CdTe, single-junction GaAs) are omitted rather than guessed. Numbers from 2025 onward move fast; see state-of-the-field.json.","units":"percent (power conversion efficiency); year (CE); cm² (area)","sources":["nrel-cell-efficiency-chart","green-tables-66","green-tables-67","green-tables-68","chapin-1954","kojima-2009","longi-tandem-2026"],"license":"CC BY 4.0 (Solar Odyssey compilation; values are facts from the cited sources)","last_verified":"2026-10-02"},"data":{"series":[{"id":"si-mono","label":"Crystalline silicon","short":"Silicon","family":"silicon","colour":"--t-silicon","limit":29.4,"limit_source":"richter-2013","note":"Single-crystal silicon, one sun. Includes heterojunction and back-contact designs."},{"id":"cigs","label":"CIGS thin film","short":"CIGS","family":"thinfilm","colour":"--t-thinfilm","limit":null,"limit_source":null,"note":"Copper indium gallium selenide."},{"id":"perovskite","label":"Perovskite","short":"Perovskite","family":"perovskite","colour":"--t-perovskite","limit":null,"limit